meta {
  name: Complete Onboarding
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{apiUrl}}/users/me/onboarding
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "fullName": "Host user 1",
    "skillLevel": 3
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.success: eq true
  res.body.data.onboarded: eq true
  res.body.data.fullName: eq Host user 1
  res.body.data.skillLevel: eq 3
}

docs {
  `CompleteOnboardingUseCase` -> `UserRepository.completeOnboarding`: one `UpdateCommand` that sets
  name + level and `onboarded_at = if_not_exists(onboarded_at, :now)`. PATCH, like `PATCH
  /users/me` -- both update the user resource, this one just requires both fields and also sets
  `onboarded_at` as a side effect of completing the step.

  Idempotent on purpose: running this again is a harmless edit and keeps the first timestamp.

  Note: this onboards whichever account the Auth folder signed in as (the host test user), with the
  same name/level the other User requests already use. Use the *player* account to try the
  onboarding screen in the browser.
}
